.TH BURNCRACKER 1 "2026-08-09" "Burn Suite 1.0" "Burn Suite Manual"
.SH NAME
burncracker \- automated WiFi handshake capture and password cracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo python3 ./burncracker.py
.br
.B sudo burncracker
.RI ( "if installed via " install.sh )
.br
.B python3 ./burncracker.py --check
.RI ( "dependency preflight only; does not require root" )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B burncracker
puts a wireless interface into monitor mode, scans for nearby WPA/WPA2
networks, captures a 4\-way handshake from a chosen target (optionally
forcing one via deauthentication), and attempts to crack the resulting
passphrase against a wordlist using either aircrack\-ng (CPU) or
hashcat (GPU, optionally with mutation rules).
.PP
Must be run as root. Requires a physical wireless adapter with monitor
mode support \- it will not work inside most VMs unless a USB WiFi
adapter is passed through directly to the guest.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B aircrack\-ng suite
airodump\-ng, aireplay\-ng, aircrack\-ng \- all required.
.RB ( airmon\-ng
is not used \- see
.B ADAPTER SELECTION
below.)
.TP
.B iw
Required \- used to enumerate wireless interfaces and switch the
selected one into/out of monitor mode.
.TP
.B NetworkManager / nmcli
Optional. If present, used to cleanly release just the selected
interface from NetworkManager's control (and hand it back afterward)
without touching any other interface. If absent, this step is skipped
gracefully \- there's nothing to isolate from.
.TP
.B hashcat
Optional, for GPU\-accelerated cracking (methods 2 and 3). Falls back
to aircrack\-ng automatically if not found.
.TP
.B hcxtools
Optional, for converting captures to hashcat's format.
.TP
.B OUI database
Optional. If an OUI/MAC\-prefix database is present \-
.I /usr/share/nmap/nmap\-mac\-prefixes
(from
.BR nmap )
or
.I /usr/share/ieee\-data/oui.txt
(from
.BR ieee\-data )
\- the connected\-device list shows each client's hardware vendor to help
you pick a target. If absent, clients are still listed but without a
vendor name. No network lookups are ever performed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Run the dependency preflight and exit. Reports each required tool
.RB ( airodump\-ng ", " aireplay\-ng ", " aircrack\-ng ", " iw )
and optional one
.RB ( hashcat ", " hcxtools ", " hcxdumptool ", " "OUI database" )
as present or missing, then exits 0 if all required tools are present
or 2 if any are missing (logged as \fBCRACK\-104\fR). Does not require
root and performs no scanning \- useful for verifying a machine is
ready before an engagement.
.SH USAGE
.TP
.B 0.
On every normal run the same preflight runs first; a missing required
tool aborts before any prompts (exit 2).
.TP
.B 1.
The tool checks for a VM (warns and asks to confirm before continuing
if detected). The wordlist is
.B not
chosen here \- you pick it later, at crack time (step 7), so you're
never prompted for one unless a handshake is actually captured. See
.B WORDLISTS
below.
.TP
.B 2.
Every wireless interface on the system is listed (via
.BR "iw dev" ),
each with a best\-effort driver\-name hint, and you pick which one to
dedicate to this run \- e.g. a USB adapter, so your main connection is
left completely alone. See
.B ADAPTER SELECTION
below.
.TP
.B 3.
Monitor mode starts automatically on the
.B selected
interface only.
.TP
.B 4.
It scans all channels for \fBSCAN_SECONDS\fR (default 20s) and lists
nearby networks with SSID, BSSID, channel, encryption, and a
best\-effort device hint. Because the scan hops channels quickly it
rarely catches client frames, so the DEVICES column shows a dash
(\(dq\(em\(dq) when none were seen \- this means \(dqnone seen in the
quick scan\(dq, not \(dqconfirmed empty\(dq. Exact clients are counted
in step 6 once a target is chosen and the card dwells on its channel.
.TP
.B 5.
Select a target network. The tool classifies its security and only
proceeds when there is actually something to attack (see
.B WPA3 AND WHAT IS ATTACKABLE
below): open (OPN), WPA/WPA2-Enterprise, and WPA3-only (SAE) targets
are declined with an explanation; WPA/WPA2-PSK and WPA3 transition
mode proceed.
.TP
.B 6.
Choose a capture method. If
.B hcxdumptool
is installed you are offered
.B PMKID
(clientless \- request the PMKID straight from the AP, no client and
no deauth, so it's quiet) or
.B handshake
(below); otherwise it goes straight to the handshake method. For the
handshake method, connected clients are listed, each annotated with
its hardware vendor (via OUI lookup) so you can pick a specific device
\- a randomized MAC is flagged as a likely phone, while a named vendor
(e.g. an IoT maker) is usually the least\-noticed thing to knock off.
Choose whether to deauth a single device, deauth all devices (requires
typing \fBCONFIRM\fR \- this disconnects everyone on the network), or
wait passively. A single\-device deauth is sent as
.B targeted (unicast)
frames to that client only \- no broadcast frames \- to stay as covert
as possible. If no devices are seen, you can wait indefinitely, pick a
different target, or capture passively anyway.
.TP
.B 7.
Once a handshake is captured, choose a cracking method:
.RS
.IP 1. 3
Aircrack\-ng (CPU) \- slowest, works everywhere.
.IP 2. 3
Hashcat (GPU) \- much faster, requires a compatible GPU.
.IP 3. 3
Hashcat + rules (GPU) \- mutates the wordlist for broader coverage.
.RE
.IP
After the method is chosen you are prompted for the wordlist \- one of
the installed lists under \fI/usr/share/wordlists\fR (shown with sizes,
rockyou.txt offered as the default) or a custom path you type in.
Gzipped lists are decompressed automatically. All three methods run a
dictionary attack, so this prompt applies to hashcat as well as
aircrack.
.IP
The cracker's live output is streamed to the terminal as it runs, with
a periodic elapsed\-time heartbeat during quiet stretches, so a long
run shows continuous progress instead of a blank screen. Interrupting
with Ctrl+C stops the cracker cleanly rather than leaving it running in
the background.
.TP
.B 8.
Results are written to \fIburn_report/burncracker_<timestamp>.txt\fR
and the selected interface is restored to normal (managed) mode \-
even if something fails partway through, a crash cannot leave the
adapter stuck in monitor mode, and every other interface was never
touched in the first place.
.SH ADAPTER SELECTION
No interface is hardcoded. Each run,
.B burncracker.py
lists every wireless interface found via
.B "iw dev"
and lets you pick one \- ideal for dedicating a secondary USB adapter
(e.g. an Alfa AWUS036ACH or AWUS036ACM) to this tool's work while your
main/built\-in card stays connected to whatever network you're already
on. Only the interface you pick is ever released from NetworkManager
or switched into monitor mode \- every other interface, including
whatever's keeping you online, is left completely alone.
.PP
This replaces the old
.B airmon\-ng
based approach, which killed NetworkManager and wpa_supplicant
system\-wide and would disconnect every wireless connection on the
machine, not just the target adapter.
.SH WORDLISTS
You pick the wordlist interactively at crack time \- after a handshake
is captured and a method is chosen (step 7), not at startup. The tool
scans
.B WORDLIST_DIR
(default \fI/usr/share/wordlists\fR) for \fI.txt\fR/\fI.lst\fR files
(including \fI.gz\fR variants), lists them with their sizes, offers
.B WORDLIST
(default \fI/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt\fR) as the recommended
first pass, and also accepts a custom path you type in \- so a larger
list (e.g. SecLists, CrackStation) needs no code change. A chosen
gzipped list is decompressed automatically (the original \fI.gz\fR is
kept).
.SH WPA3 AND WHAT IS ATTACKABLE
The capture\-and\-crack model this tool uses is an
.B offline dictionary attack:
capture a WPA2\-PSK 4\-way handshake (or a PMKID), then try passphrases
against it offline at GPU speed. That works because the handshake
yields a verifier you can test guesses against.
.PP
.B WPA3\-Personal replaces PSK authentication with SAE
(Simultaneous Authentication of Equals), a password\-authenticated key
exchange
.B designed specifically to defeat offline dictionary attacks.
Capturing a SAE handshake does not give you anything to test passwords
against offline \- there is no hashcat mode for it \- so a WPA3\-only
network is
.B not crackable this way regardless of hardware
(a laptop, a GPU farm, and a datacenter are equally stuck). The tool
detects this and declines with \fBCRACK\-403\fR rather than wasting
your time. AES/CCMP is only the cipher; SAE is the barrier.
.PP
The practical exception is
.B WPA3 transition mode
\- a mixed network that offers both WPA2 and WPA3 for compatibility. A
client that connects over WPA2/PSK still produces a crackable
handshake, so those targets proceed via the WPA2 path.
WPA/WPA2\-Enterprise (802.1X/EAP) has no pre\-shared key to attack and
is declined with \fBCRACK\-404\fR.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit the constants near the top of \fBburncracker.py\fR:
.TP
.B WORDLIST
Path offered as the default/recommended wordlist. Default
\fI/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt\fR.
.TP
.B WORDLIST_DIR
Directory scanned for installed wordlists to offer in the menu.
Default \fI/usr/share/wordlists\fR.
.TP
.B SCAN_SECONDS
How long to scan for networks before showing the list. Default 20.
.PP
The wireless adapter itself is not a config constant \- it's chosen
interactively each run (see
.B ADAPTER SELECTION
above).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed normally (cracked or not \- check the report's STATUS field).
.TP
.B 1
User cancelled (declined VM warning, network is open, etc).
.TP
.B 2
Environment/dependency problem (not root, wordlist unresolvable, no
wireless interface found, monitor mode failed to start).
.TP
.B 3
No usable data produced (no networks found, no handshake captured).
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Every failure, skip, or empty result is logged to the console and to
the report's DIAGNOSTICS section as a \fBCRACK\-NNN\fR code. See
.I ERROR_CODES.txt
in the suite root for the full reference. Notably: a cracking attempt
that times out or fails to complete is
.B never
reported as "password not found" \- those are logged as distinct,
inconclusive codes so a real wordlist\-exhaustion result can't be
confused with an incomplete one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I burn_report/burncracker_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt
Generated report for each run.
.TP
.I /tmp/burncracker/
Scratch directory for scan/capture files.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.B FOR AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY.
Only attack networks you own or have explicit written permission to
test. Broadcast deauthentication disconnects every device on the
network and requires a separate typed confirmation for that reason.
Unauthorized use is a federal crime under the CFAA and equivalent laws
worldwide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR burnscanner (1),
.BR burnrecon (1),
.BR burnweb (1),
.BR burnreport (1),
.BR burnsuite (7),
.BR aircrack\-ng (1),
.BR hashcat (1)
